g of potash. The Nitrogen segment owns and operates ammonia production facilities that offers ammonia, urea, ammonium nitrate (UAN), urea solutions, nitric acid, and ammonium nitrate, as well as environmentally smart nitrogen and ammonium sulfate. The Phosphate segment manufactures and sells solid and liquid phosphate fertilizers, phosphate feed, and purified phosphoric acid, which is used in feed and industrial products. The company was incorporated in 2017 and is headquartered in Saskatoon, Canada.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kenneth A. Seitz | President, CEO & Non-Independent Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Nutrien Ltd. is a large-cap basic materials business with a $33.8B market cap on $26.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -11% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 29%.","The business throws off $2.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.74\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.4\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 30% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3035718635401523},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Basic Materials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Environmental remediation liability \u2014 tightening regulations on emissions, tailings, and water use create open-ended balance-sheet risk that grows with each legislative cycle.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Financial quality scores above most Basic Materials peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Discipline and Rules-Based Execution in NTR Response","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/24/Discipline_and_Rules-Based_Execution_in_NTR_Response_111226063802_1794526682.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794526682.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Nutrien (NYSE:NTR) Stock Price Target Raised at UBS Group","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/nutrien-nysentr-stock-price-target-raised-at-ubs-group.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794496379.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.318,"t